{%- doc -%}
  Renders the inline validation message under a field's underline. Renders nothing if no message.

  @param {string} message - The message to display. Omitted or blank renders nothing.
  @param {string} [id] - Element id, for a control's aria-describedby.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Mirrors ../design-system/src/react/FormError/FormError.tsx -- the inline validation message that
  sits under a field's underline.

  FormError.tsx renders `<Text as="p" variant="label">`, and so does this. Like the React component it renders nothing at all when there is no
  message: FormField/Checkbox place it inside a flex column with a gap, so an empty <p> would still
  consume a gap and push the underline down.

  Accepts:
    message  Required to render anything. Omitted or blank renders nothing.
    id       Optional. Set it when a control points at this message with aria-describedby.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if message != blank -%}
  {%- capture error_attributes -%}{% if id != blank %}id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- render 'mionas-text',
    content: message,
    variant: 'label',
    color: 'inherit',
    tag: 'p',
    class: 'mionas-form-error',
    attributes: error_attributes
  -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* FormError.module.css .root -- padding-left keeps the message on the same optical start edge as
     the label and the input, all three of which are inset from the underline's full width. */
  .text-role.mionas-form-error {
    padding-left: var(--form-error-base-padding);
    color: var(--form-error-base-foreground);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
